    "description": "NOW Sports Whey Isolate is the value isolate for bulk buyers. The unflavored 5 lb tub lists 24 g of protein in 110 calories per 28 g scoop, with about 1 g of carbohydrate and no sweetener, per the label at the time of writing, and flavored versions are listed in 10 lb sizes. Isolate keeps a little better than concentrate because it has less fat and lactose. NOW lists Informed Sport on the label; check the certifier's database for the exact product and size you buy.",
    "pros": [
      "24 g of protein in 110 calories per scoop, per the label",
      "Isolate with very little lactose or fat",
      "Unflavored 5 lb and flavored 10 lb sizes"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Unflavored tastes faintly milky on its own",
      "Costs more per 25 g than concentrates",
      "Flavored 10 lb tubs are a big commitment to one flavor"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The bulk choice if you want isolate for lactose or macros without paying premium-brand prices.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein / serving": "24 g (label)",
      "Largest size": "5 lb unflavored; 10 lb flavored",
      "Cost per 25 g tier": "Mid",
      "Best for": "Lactose-sensitive bulk buyers"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "nutricost-whey-protein-concentrate",
    "name": "Nutricost Whey Protein Concentrate",
    "brand": "Nutricost",
    "badge": "Best Budget Bulk Whey",
    "category": "Whey protein concentrate",
    "description": "Nutricost is a value brand with a large Amazon presence, and its 5 lb whey concentrate is one of the lowest-cost ways to buy a branded whey in bulk. Retailer listings for the milk chocolate concentrate show 25 g of protein per 36 g scoop and about 130 to 140 calories. Nutricost says its products are third-party tested and made in a GMP-compliant facility, though listings do not name the lab. Unflavored and grass-fed versions are also sold.",
